message.content:
The crash is a use-of-uninitialized-value in `each_backtrace`. Looking at the code, I can see the issue. In `each_backtrace`, the `loc` struct is declared but not fully initialized. Specifically:

```c
struct backtrace_location loc;
...
if (!ci->proc || MRB_PROC_CFUNC_P(ci->proc)) {
  if (!ci->mid) continue;
  loc.lineno = -1;
  idx = 0;
}
else {
  ...
  mrb_debug_get_position(mrb, irep, idx, &loc.lineno, &loc.filename);
}
loc.method_id = ci->mid;
```

The `loc.filename` is only set in the `else` branch via `mrb_debug_get_position`. If `mrb_debug_get_position` fails to find the position, `loc.filename` may remain uninitialized. Then later:

```c
if (!loc.filename) {
  loc.filename = "(unknown)";
}
```

This reads the uninitialized `loc.filename`. Also, `loc.method_id` is set from `ci->mid` which could be uninitialized.

Let me look at the git history to understand what changed in the regression range (202302230600 to 202302240613).

